BOLTZMANN ENTROPY CORRECTION LOG
================================================================================
Applied to ALL residues (including amino acids)

METHOD:
-------
Corrects for bias when charge states have different numbers of conformers.
Charge states with more conformers are penalized to account for the
entropic cost of selecting a specific conformer.

PROCEDURE:
1. Convert probabilities to free energies: ΔG/RT = -ln(P)
2. Add entropy penalty: ΔG_corrected/RT = ΔG_original/RT + ln(N)
   where N = number of conformers in that charge state
3. Convert back to probabilities: P_i = exp(-ΔG_corrected/RT) / Z

CONSTANTS:
R = 0.001987 kcal·K⁻¹·mol⁻¹
T = 298.0 K
RT = 0.592 kcal/mol

PENALTIES:
N=1: ln(1) = 0.000 → No penalty (0.000 kcal/mol)
N=2: ln(2) = 0.693 → Penalty = 0.410 kcal/mol
N=3: ln(3) = 1.099 → Penalty = 0.651 kcal/mol
N=4: ln(4) = 1.386 → Penalty = 0.821 kcal/mol

Amino acids excluded from correction:
(None - all residues corrected)

